+    and single hyphens; it never starts or ends with a hyphen. If
+    ``max_length`` is given, the slug is cut to at most that many characters
+    and any trailing hyphen is removed. If nothing is left, ``"n-a"`` is
+    returned.
     """
-    # Replace separators before lowercasing, so non-ASCII characters that
-    # lowercase to ASCII (e.g. the Kelvin sign "K") are still treated as
-    # separators.
-    slug = _SEPARATORS.sub("-", text).strip("-").lower()
+    slug = _SEPARATORS.sub("-", _to_ascii(text)).strip("-").lower()
     if max_length is not None:
         slug = slug[: max(max_length, 0)].rstrip("-")
     return slug or "n-a"
